      <h2>About Palace Museum</h2>
      <div>Beit al-Sahel (Palace Museum) served as the Sultan's official residence from the late 19th century until the 1964 revolution. The palace displays royal furniture, ceremonial regalia, portraits of sultans, historical photographs, and artifacts documenting Zanzibar's sultanate era and the 1964 revolution. The building showcases classic Omani-Arab architecture with carved teak doors, ornate plasterwork, marble floors, and European-influenced chandeliers. Guided tours provide context on the sultanate's political history and the 1964 revolution.</div>
